  ],
  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 1.24,
      "text": "You broke no law."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.3,
      "end": 4.394,
      "text": "You carried your own cash through an airport."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.454,
      "end": 8.425,
      "text": "By the gate, it was gone."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.487,
      "end": 10.926,
      "text": "A retired railroad worker near Pittsburgh kept"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.927,
      "end": 13.047,
      "text": "his life savings in cash —"
    },
    {
      "start": 13.107,
      "end": 15.575,
      "text": "about eighty-two thousand dollars."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.635,
      "end": 17.394,
      "text": "His daughter carried it through an airport"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.395,
      "end": 19.658,
      "text": "to put it in the bank for him."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.718,
      "end": 21.377,
      "text": "Federal agents took every bill,"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.378,
      "end": 24.809,
      "text": "and never charged anyone with a crime."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.869,
      "end": 27.824,
      "text": "It happened to a man named Terry Rolin."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.884,
      "end": 28.983,
      "text": "It could happen with money"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.984,
      "end": 33.013,
      "text": "that is entirely your own."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.217,
      "end": 34.816,
      "text": "It is late August, 2019,"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.817,
      "end": 37.704,
      "text": "at Pittsburgh International Airport."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.764,
      "end": 40.263,
      "text": "A woman named Rebecca Brown walks toward her gate"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.264,
      "end": 42.264,
      "text": "with a carry-on over her shoulder,"
    },
    {
      "start": 42.304,
      "end": 44.806,
      "text": "running an errand for her father."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.866,
      "end": 47.305,
      "text": "A TSA X-ray machine sees something dense"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.306,
      "end": 49.493,
      "text": "in her bag and stops her."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.553,
      "end": 51.333,
      "text": "When a screener opens the bag,"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.393,
      "end": 52.981,
      "text": "there is no weapon inside —"
    },
    {
      "start": 52.993,
      "end": 56.053,
      "text": "only cash, bundled in bank bands,"
    },
    {
      "start": 56.113,
      "end": 58.174,
      "text": "thousands of dollars of it."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.234,
      "end": 61.058,
      "text": "To understand how that cash ended up in her bag,"
    },
    {
      "start": 61.114,
      "end": 62.734,
      "text": "back up a few miles,"
    },
    {
      "start": 62.794,
      "end": 65.333,
      "text": "to a small house near Pittsburgh where her father"
    },
    {
      "start": 65.334,
      "end": 67.412,
      "text": "had packed it that morning."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.472,
      "end": 69.684,
      "text": "His name is Terry Rolin."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.744,
      "end": 71.464,
      "text": "He is about seventy-nine,"
    },
    {
      "start": 71.524,
      "end": 74.003,
      "text": "a retired railroad worker, and for most"
    },
    {
      "start": 74.004,
      "end": 76.971,
      "text": "of his life he did not trust banks."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.031,
      "end": 78.23,
      "text": "He had lived through decades"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.231,
      "end": 79.75,
      "text": "when a bank could feel less safe"
    },
    {
      "start": 79.751,
      "end": 81.411,
      "text": "than a coffee can —"
    },
    {
      "start": 81.471,
      "end": 83.29,
      "text": "the kind of caution you might recognize"
    },
    {
      "start": 83.291,
      "end": 85.271,
      "text": "in your own parents —"
    },
    {
      "start": 85.331,
      "end": 87.15,
      "text": "so he kept his money where he could count it"
    },
    {
      "start": 87.151,
      "end": 88.577,
      "text": "himself."
    },
    {
      "start": 88.637,
      "end": 89.736,
      "text": "By that summer it came"
    },
    {
      "start": 89.737,
      "end": 93.171,
      "text": "to roughly eighty-two thousand dollars in bills."
    },
    {
      "start": 93.231,
      "end": 97.071,
      "text": "By his family's account it was everything he had,"
    },
    {
      "start": 97.131,
      "end": 98.971,
      "text": "the whole of a working life,"
    },
    {
      "start": 99.031,
      "end": 101.666,
      "text": "counted by hand and kept at home."
    },
    {
      "start": 101.726,
      "end": 103.566,
      "text": "Then came an ordinary problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 103.626,
      "end": 104.645,
      "text": "the kind you might face"
    },
    {
      "start": 104.646,
      "end": 106.864,
      "text": "with your own aging parent."
    },
    {
      "start": 106.924,
      "end": 108.943,
      "text": "Cash in a house can be lost or burned"
    },
    {
      "start": 108.944,
      "end": 112.201,
      "text": "or stolen, and Terry was getting older."
    },
    {
      "start": 112.261,
      "end": 114.937,
      "text": "So the family made a plain decision."
    },
    {
      "start": 114.997,
      "end": 117.337,
      "text": "Rebecca, who lives in another state,"
    },
    {
      "start": 117.397,
      "end": 118.896,
      "text": "would carry the money home,"
    },
    {
      "start": 118.897,
      "end": 120.557,
      "text": "open a joint bank account,"
    },
    {
      "start": 120.617,
      "end": 122.816,
      "text": "and use it to manage his finances and pay"
    },
    {
      "start": 122.817,
      "end": 125.011,
      "text": "for what he was going to need."
    },
    {
      "start": 125.071,
      "end": 128.444,
      "text": "The whole plan was to deposit it and protect it."
    },
    {
      "start": 128.504,
      "end": 131.691,
      "text": "And carrying that cash was completely legal."
    },
    {
      "start": 131.751,
      "end": 133.61,
      "text": "On a domestic flight there is no limit"
    },
    {
      "start": 133.611,
      "end": 135.11,
      "text": "on how much money you can bring,"
    },
    {
      "start": 135.111,
      "end": 138.421,
      "text": "and nothing you are required to declare."
    },
    {
      "start": 138.481,
      "end": 139.801,
      "text": "Under federal law,"
    },
    {
      "start": 139.861,
      "end": 142.12,
      "text": "the only time you must report cash is when you"
    },
    {
      "start": 142.121,
      "end": 145.961,
      "text": "carry more than ten thousand dollars across"
    },
    {
      "start": 146.021,
      "end": 149.018,
      "text": "a national border — not a state line, an international border."
    },
    {
      "start": 149.019,
      "end": 151.118,
      "text": "Rebecca was flying from one American city"
    },
    {
      "start": 151.119,
      "end": 152.199,
      "text": "to another,"
    },
    {
      "start": 152.259,
      "end": 155.132,
      "text": "well within every rule that applied to her."
    },
    {
      "start": 155.192,
      "end": 157.133,
      "text": "The next time you fly with cash —"
    },
    {
      "start": 157.172,
      "end": 160.452,
      "text": "for a car, a house deposit, a gift to family —"
    },
    {
      "start": 160.512,
      "end": 162.252,
      "text": "the same rule protects you:"
    },
    {
      "start": 162.312,
      "end": 163.492,
      "text": "it is your money,"
    },
    {
      "start": 163.552,
      "end": 165.851,
      "text": "and no law says you owe anyone an explanation"
    },
    {
      "start": 165.852,
      "end": 167.574,
      "text": "for carrying it."
    },
    {
      "start": 167.634,
      "end": 170.264,
      "text": "But cash tends to summon people."
    },
    {
      "start": 170.324,
      "end": 172.043,
      "text": "A Pennsylvania state trooper came"
    },
    {
      "start": 172.044,
      "end": 174.323,
      "text": "to the checkpoint, and then a federal agent"
    },
    {
      "start": 174.324,
      "end": 176.223,
      "text": "from the Drug Enforcement Administration,"
    },
    {
      "start": 176.224,
      "end": 178.663,
      "text": "identified in the court filings only"
    },
    {
      "start": 178.664,
      "end": 180.616,
      "text": "by a first name."
    },
    {
      "start": 180.676,
      "end": 182.335,
      "text": "They questioned Rebecca at the gate"
    },
    {
      "start": 182.336,
      "end": 184.435,
      "text": "while strangers counted her father's savings"
    },
    {
      "start": 184.436,
      "end": 187.578,
      "text": "into stacks of hundred-dollar bands."
    },
    {
      "start": 187.638,
      "end": 190.618,
      "text": "They called Terry, half-asleep back in Pittsburgh,"
    },
    {
      "start": 190.678,
      "end": 193.24,
      "text": "and asked him about the money too."
    },
    {
      "start": 193.3,
      "end": 194.199,
      "text": "Afterward they said"
    },
    {
      "start": 194.2,
      "end": 196.719,
      "text": "the two accounts did not match."
    },
    {
      "start": 196.779,
      "end": 198.434,
      "text": "So they took it."
    },
    {
      "start": 198.494,
      "end": 201.573,
      "text": "The entire eighty-two thousand dollars,"
    },
    {
      "start": 201.574,
      "end": 203.033,
      "text": "seized on the spot and carried away"
    },
    {
      "start": 203.034,
      "end": 205.734,
      "text": "in an envelope."
    },
    {
      "start": 205.794,
      "end": 206.799,
      "text": "They found no drugs."
    },
    {
      "start": 206.8,
      "end": 207.824,
      "text": "They made no arrest."
    },
    {
      "start": 207.825,
      "end": 209.704,
      "text": "Neither Terry nor Rebecca was charged"
    },
    {
      "start": 209.705,
      "end": 212.777,
      "text": "with any crime, then or later."
    },
    {
      "start": 212.837,
      "end": 215.316,
      "text": "His life savings were gone in a single afternoon,"
    },
    {
      "start": 215.317,
      "end": 218.346,
      "text": "and the money was simply gone."
    },
    {
      "start": 218.406,
      "end": 220.618,
      "text": "Which leaves one question."
    },
    {
      "start": 220.678,
      "end": 222.358,
      "text": "If there was no crime,"
    },
    {
      "start": 222.418,
      "end": 224.515,
      "text": "how was any of this legal?"
    },
    {
      "start": 224.575,
      "end": 226.274,
      "text": "The answer is not one agent having"
    },
    {
      "start": 226.275,
      "end": 228.134,
      "text": "a bad afternoon."
    },
    {
      "start": 228.194,
      "end": 230.018,
      "text": "It is a system Congress built —"
    },
    {
      "start": 230.074,
      "end": 231.853,
      "text": "and one its critics say runs largely"
    },
    {
      "start": 231.854,
      "end": 235.648,
      "text": "on its own incentives."
    },
    {
      "start": 235.895,
      "end": 238.757,
      "text": "What happened to Terry Rolin has a name."
    },
    {
      "start": 238.817,
      "end": 241.117,
      "text": "It is called civil asset forfeiture,"
    },
    {
      "start": 241.177,
      "end": 242.916,
      "text": "and it is one of the strangest powers"
    },
    {
      "start": 242.917,
      "end": 244.79,
      "text": "the government holds."
    },
    {
      "start": 244.85,
      "end": 247.619,
      "text": "Most people never learn it exists."
    },
    {
      "start": 247.679,
      "end": 249.738,
      "text": "It begins with a legal move that sounds like"
    },
    {
      "start": 249.739,
      "end": 251.238,
      "text": "a typo."
    },
    {
      "start": 251.298,
      "end": 253.238,
      "text": "In an ordinary criminal case,"
    },
    {
      "start": 253.298,
      "end": 255.646,
      "text": "the government charges a person."
    },
    {
      "start": 255.706,
      "end": 256.685,
      "text": "In civil forfeiture,"
    },
    {
      "start": 256.686,
      "end": 259.426,
      "text": "the government sues the property itself —"
    },
    {
      "start": 259.486,
      "end": 261.772,
      "text": "the money becomes the defendant."
    },
    {
      "start": 261.832,
      "end": 263.871,
      "text": "That is why these cases carry captions"
    },
    {
      "start": 263.872,
      "end": 266.052,
      "text": "that read like a joke but are not,"
    },
    {
      "start": 266.112,
      "end": 268.451,
      "text": "something like \"the United States versus a pile"
    },
    {
      "start": 268.452,
      "end": 270.252,
      "text": "of cash.\""
    },
    {
      "start": 270.312,
      "end": 272.253,
      "text": "Lawyers call it an action in rem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 272.272,
      "end": 273.936,
      "text": "against the thing."
    },
    {
      "start": 273.996,
      "end": 275.695,
      "text": "Because the case is against the money"
    },
    {
      "start": 275.696,
      "end": 277.176,
      "text": "and not against you,"
    },
    {
      "start": 277.236,
      "end": 279.275,
      "text": "the government does not have to charge you,"
    },
    {
      "start": 279.276,
      "end": 280.256,
      "text": "or convict you,"
    },
    {
      "start": 280.316,
      "end": 283.592,
      "text": "or even say out loud that you did anything wrong."
    },
    {
      "start": 283.652,
      "end": 285.251,
      "text": "For a long time that left owners"
    },
    {
      "start": 285.252,
      "end": 288.072,
      "text": "in an almost impossible spot:"
    },
    {
      "start": 288.132,
      "end": 290.431,
      "text": "once the government seized your property,"
    },
    {
      "start": 290.432,
      "end": 291.331,
      "text": "the burden was on you"
    },
    {
      "start": 291.332,
      "end": 293.944,
      "text": "to prove your own money was innocent."
    },
    {
      "start": 294.004,
      "end": 296.303,
      "text": "In the year 2000, Congress changed"
    },
    {
      "start": 296.304,
      "end": 299.186,
      "text": "that with the Civil Asset Forfeiture Reform Act —"
    },
    {
      "start": 299.244,
      "end": 300.488,
      "text": "CAFRA."
    },
    {
      "start": 300.548,
      "end": 302.508,
      "text": "On paper it flipped the scale,"
    },
    {
      "start": 302.568,
      "end": 304.047,
      "text": "so now the government has to prove"
    },
    {
      "start": 304.048,
      "end": 305.788,
      "text": "the property is forfeitable."
    },
    {
      "start": 305.848,
      "end": 307.915,
      "text": "But read the fine print."
    },
    {
      "start": 307.975,
      "end": 310.054,
      "text": "The standard is only a \"preponderance"
    },
    {
      "start": 310.055,
      "end": 311.014,
      "text": "of the evidence\" —"
    },
    {
      "start": 311.015,
      "end": 312.88,
      "text": "more likely than not."
    },
    {
      "start": 312.94,
      "end": 315.179,
      "text": "That is the bar your own savings would be judged"
    },
    {
      "start": 315.18,
      "end": 317.659,
      "text": "by, and it sits far below the \"beyond"
    },
    {
      "start": 317.66,
      "end": 320.239,
      "text": "a reasonable doubt\" a prosecutor needs"
    },
    {
      "start": 320.24,
      "end": 322.443,
      "text": "to put someone in prison."
    },
    {
      "start": 322.503,
      "end": 323.883,
      "text": "In plain terms,"
    },
    {
      "start": 323.943,
      "end": 325.882,
      "text": "the government does not have to be sure your money"
    },
    {
      "start": 325.883,
      "end": 327.362,
      "text": "is dirty."
    },
    {
      "start": 327.422,
      "end": 328.961,
      "text": "It only has to convince a judge"
    },
    {
      "start": 328.962,
      "end": 331.77,
      "text": "that it is more likely dirty than not."
    },
    {
      "start": 331.83,
      "end": 334.35,
      "text": "Most people never fight at all:"
    },
    {
      "start": 334.41,
      "end": 335.949,
      "text": "the cash they lost is worth less"
    },
    {
      "start": 335.95,
      "end": 338.229,
      "text": "than the lawyer it would take to get it back,"
    },
    {
      "start": 338.23,
      "end": 340.125,
      "text": "so they let it go."
    },
    {
      "start": 340.185,
      "end": 341.604,
      "text": "So why would an agency reach"
    },
    {
      "start": 341.605,
      "end": 344.325,
      "text": "for this when there is no crime to prosecute?"
    },
    {
      "start": 344.385,
      "end": 345.88,
      "text": "Follow the money."
    },
    {
      "start": 345.94,
      "end": 348.88,
      "text": "Under a federal program called equitable sharing,"
    },
    {
      "start": 348.94,
      "end": 351.34,
      "text": "rooted in a 1984 crime law,"
    },
    {
      "start": 351.4,
      "end": 353.939,
      "text": "the agency that seizes the cash can keep or share"
    },
    {
      "start": 353.94,
      "end": 355.582,
      "text": "the proceeds."
    },
    {
      "start": 355.642,
      "end": 358.365,
      "text": "It does not vanish into the Treasury."
    },
    {
      "start": 358.425,
      "end": 360.384,
      "text": "It can flow straight back to the office"
    },
    {
      "start": 360.385,
      "end": 361.225,
      "text": "that took it —"
    },
    {
      "start": 361.285,
      "end": 361.944,
      "text": "so the office"
    },
    {
      "start": 361.945,
      "end": 363.984,
      "text": "that emptied your bag can spend what it found"
    },
    {
      "start": 363.985,
      "end": 365.234,
      "text": "there."
    },
    {
      "start": 365.294,
      "end": 367.074,
      "text": "The Institute for Justice,"
    },
    {
      "start": 367.134,
      "end": 368.993,
      "text": "the public-interest law firm at the center"
    },
    {
      "start": 368.994,
      "end": 370.214,
      "text": "of this story,"
    },
    {
      "start": 370.274,
      "end": 372.373,
      "text": "argues that this builds a financial incentive"
    },
    {
      "start": 372.374,
      "end": 375.854,
      "text": "to seize, and a way around stricter state laws,"
    },
    {
      "start": 375.914,
      "end": 378.073,
      "text": "since federal sharing can pay out even where"
    },
    {
      "start": 378.074,
      "end": 380.091,
      "text": "a state would say no."
    },
    {
      "start": 380.151,
      "end": 382.671,
      "text": "They are an advocate here, not a referee,"
    },
    {
      "start": 382.731,
      "end": 384.917,
      "text": "so weigh it as one side."
    },
    {
      "start": 384.977,
      "end": 387.777,
      "text": "But the loop they describe is not a theory:"
    },
    {
      "start": 387.837,
      "end": 390.417,
      "text": "seize the cash, keep the proceeds,"
    },
    {
      "start": 390.477,
      "end": 391.716,
      "text": "and the incentive is written"
    },
    {
      "start": 391.717,
      "end": 393.969,
      "text": "into the structure itself."
    },
    {
      "start": 394.029,
      "end": 396.189,
      "text": "Put those two pieces together —"
    },
    {
      "start": 396.249,
      "end": 397.608,
      "text": "a lawsuit against your money"
    },
    {
      "start": 397.609,
      "end": 399.668,
      "text": "on a more-likely-than-not standard,"
    },
    {
      "start": 399.689,
      "end": 402.429,
      "text": "and an agency that keeps what it takes —"
    },
    {
      "start": 402.489,
      "end": 405.436,
      "text": "and you have a machine with a motive to run."
    },
    {
      "start": 405.496,
      "end": 408.576,
      "text": "And it runs at a scale most people never imagine:"
    },
    {
      "start": 408.636,
      "end": 413.916,
      "text": "not a few hundred cases, but tens of thousands."
    },
    {
      "start": 414.451,
      "end": 417.174,
      "text": "Terry Rolin's case was not rare."
    },
    {
      "start": 417.234,
      "end": 418.853,
      "text": "Pull back from that one checkpoint,"
    },
    {
      "start": 418.854,
      "end": 422.557,
      "text": "and the same scene repeats across the country."
    },
    {
      "start": 422.617,
      "end": 426.017,
      "text": "In 2016, a USA Today investigation,"
    },
    {
      "start": 426.077,
      "end": 429.057,
      "text": "later cited in the coverage of Terry's own case,"
    },
    {
      "start": 429.117,
      "end": 432.577,
      "text": "reported that between 2006 and 2015"
    },
    {
      "start": 432.637,
      "end": 435.176,
      "text": "the DEA seized more than two hundred"
    },
    {
      "start": 435.177,
      "end": 436.916,
      "text": "and nine million dollars"
    },
    {
      "start": 436.917,
      "end": 439.636,
      "text": "from over five thousand travelers,"
    },
    {
      "start": 439.637,
      "end": 441.142,
      "text": "across fifteen major American airports."
    },
    {
      "start": 441.143,
      "end": 444.423,
      "text": "And Rebecca was far from alone at her own gate."
    },
    {
      "start": 444.483,
      "end": 445.623,
      "text": "At Pittsburgh,"
    },
    {
      "start": 445.683,
      "end": 447.822,
      "text": "hundreds of travelers were stopped and separated"
    },
    {
      "start": 447.823,
      "end": 450.689,
      "text": "from their cash over just a few years."
    },
    {
      "start": 450.749,
      "end": 452.496,
      "text": "Picture one of them."
    },
    {
      "start": 452.556,
      "end": 454.395,
      "text": "A traveler with a boarding pass folded"
    },
    {
      "start": 454.396,
      "end": 457.316,
      "text": "into a shirt pocket and a connection to catch,"
    },
    {
      "start": 457.376,
      "end": 458.736,
      "text": "standing at a table,"
    },
    {
      "start": 458.796,
      "end": 460.575,
      "text": "watching a stranger zip his own money"
    },
    {
      "start": 460.576,
      "end": 462.836,
      "text": "into an evidence bag —"
    },
    {
      "start": 462.896,
      "end": 465.356,
      "text": "being told, as it happened,"
    },
    {
      "start": 465.416,
      "end": 466.455,
      "text": "that he could hire a lawyer"
    },
    {
      "start": 466.456,
      "end": 468.696,
      "text": "if he ever wanted it back."
    },
    {
      "start": 468.756,
      "end": 470.636,
      "text": "By the time his flight boarded,"
    },
    {
      "start": 470.696,
      "end": 472.075,
      "text": "the cash was sealed in a bag"
    },
    {
      "start": 472.076,
      "end": 472.955,
      "text": "with a case number,"
    },
    {
      "start": 472.956,
      "end": 475.395,
      "text": "and he was left holding a receipt for money"
    },
    {
      "start": 475.396,
      "end": 477.934,
      "text": "that had been his an hour before."
    },
    {
      "start": 477.994,
      "end": 480.67,
      "text": "Those individual stories add up."
    },
    {
      "start": 480.73,
      "end": 483.849,
      "text": "In 2017, the Justice Department's own Office"
    },
    {
      "start": 483.85,
      "end": 485.129,
      "text": "of Inspector General looked"
    },
    {
      "start": 485.13,
      "end": 487.679,
      "text": "at the DEA's cash seizures."
    },
    {
      "start": 487.739,
      "end": 489.899,
      "text": "Over roughly a decade, it reported,"
    },
    {
      "start": 489.959,
      "end": 491.238,
      "text": "the agency had seized more"
    },
    {
      "start": 491.239,
      "end": 494.818,
      "text": "than three point two billion dollars in cash,"
    },
    {
      "start": 494.819,
      "end": 497.398,
      "text": "across about sixty-five thousand seizures,"
    },
    {
      "start": 497.399,
      "end": 499.935,
      "text": "none of it connected to a criminal charge."
    },
    {
      "start": 499.995,
      "end": 502.415,
      "text": "The report was careful with the word:"
    },
    {
      "start": 502.475,
      "end": 504.815,
      "text": "this money was seized, not forfeited —"
    },
    {
      "start": 504.875,
      "end": 505.795,
      "text": "taken first,"
    },
    {
      "start": 505.855,
      "end": 507.894,
      "text": "with the question of guilt left for later,"
    },
    {
      "start": 507.895,
      "end": 509.637,
      "text": "if it came at all."
    },
    {
      "start": 509.697,
      "end": 513.116,
      "text": "And behind each of those seizures is a household."
    },
    {
      "start": 513.176,
      "end": 515.175,
      "text": "When Rebecca later described what losing"
    },
    {
      "start": 515.176,
      "end": 517.016,
      "text": "the money did to her father,"
    },
    {
      "start": 517.076,
      "end": 519.276,
      "text": "she did not talk about the law."
    },
    {
      "start": 519.336,
      "end": 521.518,
      "text": "She talked about his teeth."
    },
    {
      "start": 521.578,
      "end": 522.777,
      "text": "In a public statement,"
    },
    {
      "start": 522.778,
      "end": 524.557,
      "text": "she said he had to put off dental work he"
    },
    {
      "start": 524.558,
      "end": 527.718,
      "text": "badly needed, which left him in pain for months,"
    },
    {
      "start": 527.778,
      "end": 529.877,
      "text": "and that he could not make repairs his truck"
    },
    {
      "start": 529.878,
      "end": 531.174,
      "text": "needed."
    },
    {
      "start": 531.234,
      "end": 532.853,
      "text": "That is what a forfeiture looks like"
    },
    {
      "start": 532.854,
      "end": 534.414,
      "text": "from the inside —"
    },
    {
      "start": 534.474,
      "end": 536.013,
      "text": "an old man waiting, in pain,"
    },
    {
      "start": 536.014,
      "end": 537.793,
      "text": "over money the government held"
    },
    {
      "start": 537.794,
      "end": 540.133,
      "text": "and never charged him about."
    },
    {
      "start": 540.193,
      "end": 542.812,
      "text": "By the Institute for Justice's own accounting,"
    },
    {
      "start": 542.813,
      "end": 543.132,
      "text": "states"
    },
    {
      "start": 543.133,
      "end": 545.112,
      "text": "and the federal government together have taken"
    },
    {
      "start": 545.113,
      "end": 548.192,
      "text": "at least sixty-eight point eight billion dollars"
    },
    {
      "start": 548.193,
      "end": 550.578,
      "text": "through forfeiture since the year 2000."
    },
    {
      "start": 550.638,
      "end": 551.797,
      "text": "The group is quick to say"
    },
    {
      "start": 551.798,
      "end": 553.437,
      "text": "that number is probably too low,"
    },
    {
      "start": 553.438,
      "end": 555.818,
      "text": "because the reporting is so patchy —"
    },
    {
      "start": 555.878,
      "end": 558.144,
      "text": "a floor, not a ceiling."
    },
    {
      "start": 558.204,
      "end": 560.416,
      "text": "And this is not history."
    },
    {
      "start": 560.476,
      "end": 560.975,
      "text": "Reporting"
    },
    {
      "start": 560.976,
      "end": 564.816,
      "text": "in late 2025 described new airport seizures,"
    },
    {
      "start": 564.876,
      "end": 568.679,
      "text": "still happening, still following the same pattern."
    },
    {
      "start": 568.739,
      "end": 569.539,
      "text": "In one,"
    },
    {
      "start": 569.579,
      "end": 571.918,
      "text": "agents at a Texas airport stopped a traveler"
    },
    {
      "start": 571.919,
      "end": 574.679,
      "text": "and took hundreds of thousands of dollars,"
    },
    {
      "start": 574.739,
      "end": 577.019,
      "text": "saying they smelled marijuana."
    },
    {
      "start": 577.079,
      "end": 578.419,
      "text": "None was found."
    },
    {
      "start": 578.479,
      "end": 580.471,
      "text": "No charges followed."
    },
    {
      "start": 580.531,
      "end": 582.77,
      "text": "In another, the government took a six-figure sum"
    },
    {
      "start": 582.771,
      "end": 584.031,
      "text": "from a traveler,"
    },
    {
      "start": 584.091,
      "end": 586.51,
      "text": "then settled by handing back a portion and keeping"
    },
    {
      "start": 586.511,
      "end": 587.991,
      "text": "the rest."
    },
    {
      "start": 588.051,
      "end": 589.411,
      "text": "In that second case,"
    },
    {
      "start": 589.471,
      "end": 592.01,
      "text": "no one ever showed the money was drug money;"
    },
    {
      "start": 592.011,
      "end": 594.768,
      "text": "no one proved it was anything but his."
    },
    {
      "start": 594.828,
      "end": 595.647,
      "text": "Getting even part"
    },
    {
      "start": 595.648,
      "end": 598.247,
      "text": "of it back still cost him lawyers, filings,"
    },
    {
      "start": 598.248,
      "end": 599.847,
      "text": "and months of his life,"
    },
    {
      "start": 599.848,
      "end": 603.82,
      "text": "and in the end the government simply kept a share."
    },
    {
      "start": 603.88,
      "end": 605.46,
      "text": "Not because it had won,"
    },
    {
      "start": 605.52,
      "end": 607.459,
      "text": "but because fighting to the finish is slow"
    },
    {
      "start": 607.46,
      "end": 611.34,
      "text": "and expensive, and most people cannot outlast it."
    },
    {
      "start": 611.4,
      "end": 613.899,
      "text": "Settlements like that rarely make the news,"
    },
    {
      "start": 613.9,
      "end": 615.999,
      "text": "and a judge almost never gets to say"
    },
    {
      "start": 616.0,
      "end": 617.652,
      "text": "who was right."
    },
    {
      "start": 617.712,
      "end": 620.132,
      "text": "So when Terry's family decided to fight,"
    },
    {
      "start": 620.192,
      "end": 623.175,
      "text": "they were not only fighting for their own savings."
    },
    {
      "start": 623.235,
      "end": 624.694,
      "text": "They were pulling a thread that ran"
    },
    {
      "start": 624.695,
      "end": 626.515,
      "text": "through the whole system —"
    },
    {
      "start": 626.575,
      "end": 629.555,
      "text": "thousands of travelers, billions of dollars,"
    },
    {
      "start": 629.615,
      "end": 632.506,
      "text": "almost none of it ever tied to a crime."
    },
    {
      "start": 632.566,
      "end": 636.956,
      "text": "And they were not pulling it alone."
    },
    {
      "start": 637.016,
      "end": 639.075,
      "text": "It started with a phone call to the Institute"
    },
    {
      "start": 639.076,
      "end": 640.276,
      "text": "for Justice,"
    },
    {
      "start": 640.336,
      "end": 642.755,
      "text": "the firm that had spent years challenging exactly"
    },
    {
      "start": 642.756,
      "end": 644.754,
      "text": "this kind of seizure."
    },
    {
      "start": 644.814,
      "end": 647.713,
      "text": "In early 2020 they filed a federal class action"
    },
    {
      "start": 647.714,
      "end": 649.454,
      "text": "in a Pennsylvania court:"
    },
    {
      "start": 649.514,
      "end": 650.233,
      "text": "Brown versus"
    },
    {
      "start": 650.234,
      "end": 653.295,
      "text": "the Transportation Security Administration."
    },
    {
      "start": 653.355,
      "end": 656.263,
      "text": "This time the money was not the defendant."
    },
    {
      "start": 656.323,
      "end": 658.102,
      "text": "The traveler was the plaintiff,"
    },
    {
      "start": 658.103,
      "end": 659.862,
      "text": "and the target was not one seizure"
    },
    {
      "start": 659.863,
      "end": 662.018,
      "text": "but the whole practice."
    },
    {
      "start": 662.078,
      "end": 662.897,
      "text": "First, though,"
    },
    {
      "start": 662.898,
      "end": 665.178,
      "text": "a court had to agree to even hear it —"
    },
    {
      "start": 665.238,
      "end": 666.577,
      "text": "the threshold question that,"
    },
    {
      "start": 666.578,
      "end": 668.398,
      "text": "for anyone this happens to,"
    },
    {
      "start": 668.458,
      "end": 671.674,
      "text": "decides whether you ever see your own money again."
    },
    {
      "start": 671.734,
      "end": 674.271,
      "text": "The suit made three arguments."
    },
    {
      "start": 674.331,
      "end": 677.911,
      "text": "First, that the TSA had overstepped its authority:"
    },
    {
      "start": 677.971,
      "end": 678.29,
      "text": "the law"
    },
    {
      "start": 678.291,
      "end": 680.73,
      "text": "that lets it screen your bag is about weapons,"
    },
    {
      "start": 680.731,
      "end": 682.75,
      "text": "explosives, and threats to a flight —"
    },
    {
      "start": 682.751,
      "end": 684.298,
      "text": "not cash."
    },
    {
      "start": 684.358,
      "end": 685.717,
      "text": "Second, that holding travelers"
    },
    {
      "start": 685.718,
      "end": 687.837,
      "text": "and their money without reasonable suspicion"
    },
    {
      "start": 687.838,
      "end": 690.657,
      "text": "violated the Fourth Amendment."
    },
    {
      "start": 690.717,
      "end": 693.076,
      "text": "Third, that the DEA was seizing cash"
    },
    {
      "start": 693.077,
      "end": 694.576,
      "text": "of five thousand dollars"
    },
    {
      "start": 694.577,
      "end": 696.976,
      "text": "or more without probable cause,"
    },
    {
      "start": 696.977,
      "end": 699.523,
      "text": "simply because the money was there to take."
    },
    {
      "start": 699.583,
      "end": 702.303,
      "text": "To see why getting money back is so hard,"
    },
    {
      "start": 702.363,
      "end": 704.86,
      "text": "look at what the process demands."
    },
    {
      "start": 704.92,
      "end": 706.06,
      "text": "Under CAFRA,"
    },
    {
      "start": 706.12,
      "end": 708.239,
      "text": "an owner has only a narrow window to file"
    },
    {
      "start": 708.24,
      "end": 709.18,
      "text": "a claim,"
    },
    {
      "start": 709.24,
      "end": 711.039,
      "text": "which forces the government to either bring"
    },
    {
      "start": 711.04,
      "end": 714.098,
      "text": "a real case or let the property go."
    },
    {
      "start": 714.158,
      "end": 716.638,
      "text": "Miss the deadline, or file the wrong form,"
    },
    {
      "start": 716.698,
      "end": 719.097,
      "text": "and the money can be forfeited administratively,"
    },
    {
      "start": 719.098,
      "end": 721.943,
      "text": "without a judge ever looking at it."
    },
    {
      "start": 722.003,
      "end": 723.582,
      "text": "Even when you do everything right,"
    },
    {
      "start": 723.583,
      "end": 726.283,
      "text": "the process can drag on for a year or more,"
    },
    {
      "start": 726.343,
      "end": 728.282,
      "text": "with your cash sitting in a government account"
    },
    {
      "start": 728.283,
      "end": 730.066,
      "text": "the whole time."
    },
    {
      "start": 730.126,
      "end": 731.445,
      "text": "For a family trying to pay"
    },
    {
      "start": 731.446,
      "end": 733.726,
      "text": "for an aging parent's care,"
    },
    {
      "start": 733.786,
      "end": 735.705,
      "text": "that year is not a technicality —"
    },
    {
      "start": 735.706,
      "end": 737.957,
      "text": "it is care that does not happen."
    },
    {
      "start": 738.017,
      "end": 740.097,
      "text": "It is the surgery pushed back,"
    },
    {
      "start": 740.157,
      "end": 741.797,
      "text": "the roof left unfixed,"
    },
    {
      "start": 741.857,
      "end": 743.697,
      "text": "a month of bills paid late —"
    },
    {
      "start": 743.757,
      "end": 745.216,
      "text": "all while the paperwork grinds"
    },
    {
      "start": 745.217,
      "end": 748.774,
      "text": "on and the money sits somewhere you cannot reach."
    },
    {
      "start": 748.834,
      "end": 750.994,
      "text": "Then, within weeks of the filing,"
    },
    {
      "start": 751.054,
      "end": 753.714,
      "text": "after the story reached the national press,"
    },
    {
      "start": 753.774,
      "end": 756.154,
      "text": "the DEA gave it all back."
    },
    {
      "start": 756.214,
      "end": 759.958,
      "text": "The full savings, returned in early 2020."
    },
    {
      "start": 760.018,
      "end": 761.957,
      "text": "It offered no reason for taking the money"
    },
    {
      "start": 761.958,
      "end": 764.459,
      "text": "and no reason for returning it."
    },
    {
      "start": 764.519,
      "end": 765.758,
      "text": "It never argued in court"
    },
    {
      "start": 765.759,
      "end": 767.619,
      "text": "that Terry was a drug dealer;"
    },
    {
      "start": 767.679,
      "end": 770.446,
      "text": "it did not defend the seizure at all."
    },
    {
      "start": 770.506,
      "end": 772.904,
      "text": "It just handed the money back."
    },
    {
      "start": 772.964,
      "end": 774.704,
      "text": "For Rebecca and her father,"
    },
    {
      "start": 774.764,
      "end": 777.383,
      "text": "the money coming back was not a triumph so much"
    },
    {
      "start": 777.384,
      "end": 779.402,
      "text": "as a plain relief."
    },
    {
      "start": 779.462,
      "end": 781.682,
      "text": "The joint account could finally open,"
    },
    {
      "start": 781.742,
      "end": 784.181,
      "text": "the bills could be paid, and a plan frozen"
    },
    {
      "start": 784.182,
      "end": 786.736,
      "text": "for months could start moving again."
    },
    {
      "start": 786.796,
      "end": 789.015,
      "text": "But relief for one family was not an answer"
    },
    {
      "start": 789.016,
      "end": 790.815,
      "text": "for the thousands who never get a call"
    },
    {
      "start": 790.816,
      "end": 792.584,
      "text": "from a law firm."
    },
    {
      "start": 792.644,
      "end": 794.643,
      "text": "Terry's lawyers did not drop the case,"
    },
    {
      "start": 794.644,
      "end": 797.003,
      "text": "because giving one man his savings back"
    },
    {
      "start": 797.004,
      "end": 800.382,
      "text": "does nothing for the next five thousand travelers."
    },
    {
      "start": 800.442,
      "end": 803.025,
      "text": "So the class action pressed on."
    },
    {
      "start": 803.085,
      "end": 805.544,
      "text": "The government moved to have it thrown out, and,"
    },
    {
      "start": 805.545,
      "end": 807.205,
      "text": "according to court records,"
    },
    {
      "start": 807.265,
      "end": 810.545,
      "text": "a federal court let the core of the case proceed."
    },
    {
      "start": 810.605,
      "end": 813.105,
      "text": "No one had won anything yet —"
    },
    {
      "start": 813.165,
      "end": 815.825,
      "text": "but a court had agreed to ask, out loud,"
    },
    {
      "start": 815.885,
      "end": 818.575,
      "text": "whether any of this was constitutional."
    },
    {
      "start": 818.635,
      "end": 821.4,
      "text": "Then, according to reporting on the litigation,"
    },
    {
      "start": 821.435,
      "end": 823.854,
      "text": "in 2022 the DEA reached a settlement"
    },
    {
      "start": 823.855,
      "end": 826.494,
      "text": "in that class action, agreeing to a policy"
    },
    {
      "start": 826.495,
      "end": 829.531,
      "text": "about when it may seize travelers' cash."
    },
    {
      "start": 829.591,
      "end": 832.03,
      "text": "The exact terms are worth reading directly rather"
    },
    {
      "start": 832.031,
      "end": 833.8,
      "text": "than overstating."
    },
    {
      "start": 833.86,
      "end": 836.119,
      "text": "And the settlement did not end the fight:"
    },
    {
      "start": 836.12,
      "end": 837.8,
      "text": "the case against the TSA —"
    },
    {
      "start": 837.86,
      "end": 839.439,
      "text": "the agency that flagged the money"
    },
    {
      "start": 839.44,
      "end": 840.62,
      "text": "in the first place —"
    },
    {
      "start": 840.68,
      "end": 842.155,
      "text": "kept going."
    },
    {
      "start": 842.215,
      "end": 844.375,
      "text": "So a father had his savings back,"
    },
    {
      "start": 844.435,
      "end": 845.875,
      "text": "one claim was settled,"
    },
    {
      "start": 845.935,
      "end": 849.164,
      "text": "and the case had survived a motion to dismiss."
    },
    {
      "start": 849.224,
      "end": 852.365,
      "text": "One program was beginning to change course."
    },
    {
      "start": 852.425,
      "end": 854.824,
      "text": "The checkpoints, though, were still open —"
    },
    {
      "start": 854.825,
      "end": 856.704,
      "text": "and the reckoning was only just reaching"
    },
    {
      "start": 856.705,
      "end": 860.793,
      "text": "the agencies that ran them."
    },
    {
      "start": 860.962,
      "end": 864.056,
      "text": "Stand for a moment where those travelers stood."
    },
    {
      "start": 864.116,
      "end": 865.016,
      "text": "In practice,"
    },
    {
      "start": 865.076,
      "end": 867.155,
      "text": "a so-called \"consensual\" encounter could mean"
    },
    {
      "start": 867.156,
      "end": 869.695,
      "text": "an agent stepping between you and your gate,"
    },
    {
      "start": 869.696,
      "end": 870.835,
      "text": "asking where you were going"
    },
    {
      "start": 870.836,
      "end": 873.071,
      "text": "and how much money you were carrying —"
    },
    {
      "start": 873.116,
      "end": 876.637,
      "text": "at the exact moment saying no feels impossible."
    },
    {
      "start": 876.697,
      "end": 879.652,
      "text": "You are free to walk away, in theory."
    },
    {
      "start": 879.712,
      "end": 881.172,
      "text": "In a crowded terminal,"
    },
    {
      "start": 881.232,
      "end": 883.271,
      "text": "with a flight to catch and an agent standing"
    },
    {
      "start": 883.272,
      "end": 886.672,
      "text": "over your open bag, almost no one does."
    },
    {
      "start": 886.732,
      "end": 888.472,
      "text": "You answer the questions."
    },
    {
      "start": 888.532,
      "end": 890.329,
      "text": "You let them look."
    },
    {
      "start": 890.389,
      "end": 891.208,
      "text": "You tell yourself"
    },
    {
      "start": 891.209,
      "end": 893.008,
      "text": "that cooperating is the fastest way"
    },
    {
      "start": 893.009,
      "end": 894.949,
      "text": "to make your flight —"
    },
    {
      "start": 895.009,
      "end": 896.668,
      "text": "and that instinct is exactly what"
    },
    {
      "start": 896.669,
      "end": 899.056,
      "text": "the encounter is built to use."
    },
    {
      "start": 899.116,
      "end": 902.024,
      "text": "That pressure eventually reached the top."
    },
    {
      "start": 902.084,
      "end": 903.524,
      "text": "According to reporting,"
    },
    {
      "start": 903.584,
      "end": 906.843,
      "text": "in late 2024 the Justice Department told the DEA"
    },
    {
      "start": 906.844,
      "end": 908.223,
      "text": "to suspend those encounters"
    },
    {
      "start": 908.224,
      "end": 909.983,
      "text": "at transportation hubs,"
    },
    {
      "start": 909.984,
      "end": 912.483,
      "text": "after an internal watchdog flagged serious"
    },
    {
      "start": 912.484,
      "end": 914.652,
      "text": "constitutional risks."
    },
    {
      "start": 914.712,
      "end": 917.132,
      "text": "Then, in early 2025,"
    },
    {
      "start": 917.192,
      "end": 919.711,
      "text": "the DEA shut down its airport cash operation"
    },
    {
      "start": 919.712,
      "end": 921.032,
      "text": "altogether —"
    },
    {
      "start": 921.092,
      "end": 921.571,
      "text": "the program"
    },
    {
      "start": 921.572,
      "end": 924.679,
      "text": "that had been stopping travelers like Rebecca."
    },
    {
      "start": 924.739,
      "end": 927.018,
      "text": "And the program's own numbers show why it was hard"
    },
    {
      "start": 927.019,
      "end": 928.623,
      "text": "to defend."
    },
    {
      "start": 928.683,
      "end": 931.482,
      "text": "Over about three years, by the numbers reported,"
    },
    {
      "start": 931.483,
      "end": 934.322,
      "text": "it had seized roughly twenty-two million dollars"
    },
    {
      "start": 934.323,
      "end": 936.793,
      "text": "and produced fifty-seven arrests."
    },
    {
      "start": 936.853,
      "end": 938.413,
      "text": "A great deal of cash;"
    },
    {
      "start": 938.473,
      "end": 939.993,
      "text": "very few criminal cases —"
    },
    {
      "start": 940.053,
      "end": 941.852,
      "text": "which was exactly what Terry's lawyers"
    },
    {
      "start": 941.853,
      "end": 944.127,
      "text": "had been saying all along."
    },
    {
      "start": 944.187,
      "end": 945.127,
      "text": "That gap —"
    },
    {
      "start": 945.187,
      "end": 947.847,
      "text": "millions taken against a handful of arrests —"
    },
    {
      "start": 947.907,
      "end": 950.532,
      "text": "is what finally drew scrutiny."
    },
    {
      "start": 950.592,
      "end": 952.451,
      "text": "A tool sold to the public as a weapon"
    },
    {
      "start": 952.452,
      "end": 955.532,
      "text": "against drug cartels was, at that airport,"
    },
    {
      "start": 955.592,
      "end": 957.551,
      "text": "mostly a way to take cash from travelers"
    },
    {
      "start": 957.552,
      "end": 960.095,
      "text": "who were never charged with anything."
    },
    {
      "start": 960.155,
      "end": 962.454,
      "text": "Asked to show what it had actually caught,"
    },
    {
      "start": 962.455,
      "end": 964.074,
      "text": "the people running it did not have much"
    },
    {
      "start": 964.075,
      "end": 965.618,
      "text": "of an answer."
    },
    {
      "start": 965.678,
      "end": 966.737,
      "text": "For a program pitched"
    },
    {
      "start": 966.738,
      "end": 968.698,
      "text": "as front-line drug enforcement,"
    },
    {
      "start": 968.758,
      "end": 971.559,
      "text": "that was a hard silence to explain."
    },
    {
      "start": 971.619,
      "end": 974.038,
      "text": "But shutting one program is not the same as ending"
    },
    {
      "start": 974.039,
      "end": 975.549,
      "text": "the practice."
    },
    {
      "start": 975.609,
      "end": 976.568,
      "text": "There was the traveler"
    },
    {
      "start": 976.569,
      "end": 978.408,
      "text": "whose six-figure savings were taken"
    },
    {
      "start": 978.409,
      "end": 980.909,
      "text": "and only partly returned;"
    },
    {
      "start": 980.969,
      "end": 984.648,
      "text": "his case did not close when the DEA's program did."
    },
    {
      "start": 984.708,
      "end": 987.428,
      "text": "He was still filing, still waiting,"
    },
    {
      "start": 987.488,
      "end": 988.907,
      "text": "still paying lawyers to argue"
    },
    {
      "start": 988.908,
      "end": 992.075,
      "text": "over money no one had ever tied to a crime."
    },
    {
      "start": 992.135,
      "end": 993.415,
      "text": "For people like him,"
    },
    {
      "start": 993.475,
      "end": 996.251,
      "text": "nothing about the checkpoint had changed."
    },
    {
      "start": 996.311,
      "end": 999.191,
      "text": "The program that had taken his money was gone;"
    },
    {
      "start": 999.251,
      "end": 1002.284,
      "text": "the practice that could take yours was not."
    },
    {
      "start": 1002.344,
      "end": 1004.881,
      "text": "And it was not only that one man."
    },
    {
      "start": 1004.941,
      "end": 1005.4,
      "text": "Reporting"
    },
    {
      "start": 1005.401,
      "end": 1008.721,
      "text": "through 2025 described other federal agencies,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1008.781,
      "end": 1011.31,
      "text": "inside the Department of Homeland Security,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1011.321,
      "end": 1013.68,
      "text": "still stopping travelers and seizing their cash"
    },
    {
      "start": 1013.681,
      "end": 1015.28,
      "text": "at airports."
    },
    {
      "start": 1015.34,
      "end": 1017.7,
      "text": "The badge on the jacket had changed;"
    },
    {
      "start": 1017.76,
      "end": 1019.119,
      "text": "the traveler still had to sue"
    },
    {
      "start": 1019.12,
      "end": 1021.221,
      "text": "to get legal money back."
    },
    {
      "start": 1021.281,
      "end": 1024.22,
      "text": "A hunch, a seizure, and an owner left to fight"
    },
    {
      "start": 1024.221,
      "end": 1026.465,
      "text": "for what was already theirs."
    },
    {
      "start": 1026.525,
      "end": 1029.573,
      "text": "And Terry's own lawsuit was not finished."
    },
    {
      "start": 1029.633,
      "end": 1033.092,
      "text": "Through 2025 and into 2026 the class action"
    },
    {
      "start": 1033.093,
      "end": 1035.573,
      "text": "against the TSA was still alive,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1035.633,
      "end": 1037.713,
      "text": "motions stacking on both sides,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1037.773,
      "end": 1038.732,
      "text": "a court still weighing"
    },
    {
      "start": 1038.733,
      "end": 1041.204,
      "text": "whether the practice had ever been lawful,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1041.253,
      "end": 1044.43,
      "text": "while the DEA argued that ending its program"
    },
    {
      "start": 1044.49,
      "end": 1046.888,
      "text": "made its part of the case moot."
    },
    {
      "start": 1046.948,
      "end": 1048.967,
      "text": "The constitutional question sat where it"
    },
    {
      "start": 1048.968,
      "end": 1050.108,
      "text": "had started:"
    },
    {
      "start": 1050.168,
      "end": 1051.389,
      "text": "open."
    },
    {
      "start": 1051.449,
      "end": 1054.357,
      "text": "Which brings you back to where Terry started."
    },
    {
      "start": 1054.417,
      "end": 1056.957,
      "text": "A retired railroad worker near Pittsburgh,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1057.017,
      "end": 1059.697,
      "text": "who trusted his own home more than a bank,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1059.757,
      "end": 1062.196,
      "text": "watched his life savings vanish at an airport"
    },
    {
      "start": 1062.197,
      "end": 1065.257,
      "text": "over a story a stranger did not believe."
    },
    {
      "start": 1065.317,
      "end": 1067.31,
      "text": "He was never a criminal."
    },
    {
      "start": 1067.37,
      "end": 1068.669,
      "text": "He got his money back only"
    },
    {
      "start": 1068.67,
      "end": 1070.65,
      "text": "because a law firm took his call"
    },
    {
      "start": 1070.71,
      "end": 1073.901,
      "text": "and the noise grew too loud to ignore."
    },
    {
      "start": 1073.961,
      "end": 1076.641,
      "text": "The system that took it is still standing —"
    },
    {
      "start": 1076.701,
      "end": 1078.221,
      "text": "still funded, in part,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1078.281,
      "end": 1079.74,
      "text": "by the very cash it seizes —"
    },
    {
      "start": 1079.741,
      "end": 1082.54,
      "text": "and it can still reach money that is completely,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1082.541,
      "end": 1085.923,
      "text": "provably yours."
    },
    {
      "start": 1086.26,
      "end": 1087.799,
      "text": "Your cash is legal to carry,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1087.8,
      "end": 1091.305,
      "text": "and that has never been enough to keep it safe."
    },
    {
      "start": 1091.365,
      "end": 1093.705,
      "text": "But this story did not end in defeat."
    },
    {
      "start": 1093.765,
      "end": 1096.363,
      "text": "Terry Rolin's savings came home."
    },
    {
      "start": 1096.423,
      "end": 1098.583,
      "text": "One airport program was shut down,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1098.643,
      "end": 1101.342,
      "text": "and its own scorecard showed it took far more cash"
    },
    {
      "start": 1101.343,
      "end": 1104.043,
      "text": "than it ever turned into arrests."
    },
    {
      "start": 1104.103,
      "end": 1105.879,
      "text": "That win was real."
    },
    {
      "start": 1105.939,
      "end": 1106.818,
      "text": "The larger case"
    },
    {
      "start": 1106.819,
      "end": 1109.319,
      "text": "against the TSA is still being decided,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1109.379,
      "end": 1112.516,
      "text": "and we will follow it into the next episode."
    },
    {
      "start": 1112.576,
      "end": 1114.815,
      "text": "If you want to know how far this can go,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1114.816,
      "end": 1116.436,
      "text": "stay with the series —"
    },
    {
      "start": 1116.496,
      "end": 1118.435,
      "text": "because next we follow the same machine"
    },
    {
      "start": 1118.436,
      "end": 1121.936,
      "text": "into another life it turned upside down:"
    },
    {
      "start": 1121.996,
      "end": 1122.976,
      "text": "ordinary people,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1123.036,
      "end": 1125.701,
      "text": "and the systems that can take everything"
    },
    {
      "start": 1125.761,
      "end": 1128.243,
      "text": "without ever calling it a crime."
    }
  ],
